<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>&#160;</b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>The
Adjournment Proposal - </b>To adopt and approve a proposal to adjourn the Special Meeting to a later date or dates, if necessary, to
permit further solicitation and vote of proxies if it is determined by the Company that more time is necessary or appropriate to approve
the Issuance Proposal, the Reverse Stock Split Proposal, or the Charter Amendment Proposal at the Special Meeting (the &#8220;Adjournment
Proposal&#8221;). The Adjournment Proposal was not presented at the Special Meeting since the Issuance Proposal, the Reverse Stock Split
Proposal, and the Charter Amendment Proposal received sufficient favorable votes to be adopted.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

